# Secrets

Use this Rule whenever credentials, tokens, or application passwords are involved in a SmartFlow workspace.

## Tracked `.env` Is A Deliberate Decision

- The repo-root `.env` is tracked and pushed to the private project remote. This is an accepted, deliberate project decision. Do not "fix" it: no `.gitignore` entry, no deletion, no history scrubbing, unless the user explicitly instructs it.
- `.env` lives only at the repository root — outside the deploy path — so it never reaches the server (see `webroot-safety`). Never create `.env` or `.env.*` files inside the deploy path.

## Environment Variables Only

Secrets enter commands exclusively through environment variables:

```sh
curl -sS -u "$WSO_BRIDGE_USER:$WSO_BRIDGE_APP_PASSWORD" "<site-url>/wp-json/wso/v1/status"
```

- Never paste literal secret values into commands, tracked files other than `.env`, reusable plugin content, chat, commit messages, logs, diagnostics, screenshots, or the project `docs/` layer.
- Never print or echo secret values. When a command fails, verify that the variable is set (existence check), not what it contains.
- When a new secret is needed, ask the user to add it to `.env`; record only the variable name and its purpose in `PROJECT-CONTEXT.md`.
